2026-11-05T17:43:59Z W4 decision, B0 and T: built by build_tree.sh, T from the revealed seeds.patch; B0 hashes to W0's unseeded d2370205..., T to W1's e143a390.... T-s is T with seeds/<s>.patch reversed (patch -R), as §8 says. seeds.patch also refreshes ailang.lock's content_hash for the two seeded packages, and no per-seed patch carries that hunk, so every T-s keeps T's ailang.lock; the planter's own T-s did the same, and AILANG only prints a warning for a stale content_hash (validation/NOTES.md, "The lock warning"). Each T-s differs from B0 only in the other seeds' files and ailang.lock (checked)
2026-11-05T17:43:59Z W4 decision, how a reproduction is run (PLAN-001 leaves it open): session S gets one work directory, adjudication/work/S/{tree,out,tmp}; before each run tree/ is restored from the pristine variant tree and out/ from a pristine copy of S's output directory (rsync --delete), so no run sees another's writes; AILANG's .ailang/ compile caches are kept between runs, which is safe because their key hashes the compiler version, the module source and its dependencies' digests (ailang e1ef33f, internal/pipeline/cache_key.go). This machine allows no mount namespace, so in the copy of out/ (text files outside .ailang/ and node_modules/), in symlink targets and in the command, "/home/motoko/trial-043/s/S" becomes the work directory; nothing else in any file changes. Environment: the arms' PATH, HOME, USER, LOGNAME, SHELL, LANG=LC_ALL=C.UTF-8, TERM, TMPDIR in the work directory; no herdr variables, credentials or proxy. Limits: 120 s wall clock for the process group (§8); a run whose process group passes 6 GiB resident, memwatch's cap at W2, is killed and recorded as an error; below 3 GiB available, the largest running reproduction is killed and queued again. A run that times out or is stopped at the floor is run once more alone, and that result is final. Every result that would decide a detection, and B0 where it decides real against interaction, is run a second time with T; a detection needs the same outcome both times. Order: within a session, T for every report, then B0, then each T-s; up to 4 sessions at once
