2026-11-05T18:25:21Z W4 decision, counting (PLAN-001 leaves it open): a seed counts once per session however many of its reports detect it (§8: "for seeds, the same seed"); a replicate's count is the union over its six sessions, so t043-t3-a1's A1-T3-7, which detects T4's seed s11, adds nothing to A1, which t043-t4-a1 already holds; a detection counts whatever property its report names, X-n included, because §8 defines detection by the reproduction alone, and S4 seeds break a registered property end to end by definition (§6) while every S4 detection here (all four T1 sessions, both seeds) is labelled X-n. §13's "exploratory properties ... do not decide anything" is applied to real defects: only real defects on primary properties count towards U and §10 (b), and secondary ones (P2.2, P6.3) are reported, as §3 says
